          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.stats import norm\n\ndef tpe_1d_next_candidate(xs_obs, ys_obs, candidates, gamma: float = 0.25) -> tuple[float, float, float]:\n    xs = np.asarray(xs_obs, dtype=float)\n    ys = np.asarray(ys_obs, dtype=float)\n    cands = np.asarray(candidates, dtype=float)\n    order = np.argsort(ys)\n    n_good = max(2, int(np.ceil(gamma * len(ys))))\n    y_star = float(ys[order[n_good - 1]])\n    good_x = xs[order[:n_good]]\n    bad_x = xs[order[n_good:]]\n    bw_g = max(0.05, 1.06 * float(np.std(good_x, ddof=1)) * (len(good_x) ** -0.2))\n    bw_b = max(0.05, 1.06 * float(np.std(bad_x, ddof=1)) * (len(bad_x) ** -0.2))\n    l_pdf = (norm.pdf((cands[:, None] - good_x[None, :]) / bw_g).sum(axis=1) / bw_g + 1.0) / (len(good_x) + 1.0)\n    g_pdf = (norm.pdf((cands[:, None] - bad_x[None, :]) / bw_b).sum(axis=1) / bw_b + 1.0) / (len(bad_x) + 1.0)\n    ratios = l_pdf / np.maximum(g_pdf, 1e-12)\n    best_i = int(np.argmax(ratios))\n    return (round(float(cands[best_i]), 4), round(float(ratios[best_i]), 4), round(y_star, 4))\n```"
